PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The chemical probe is a HaloTag-reactive chloroalkane conjugated to Cy5 (excited at 630 nm, Wavelength 1), selectively labeling the *Lyz: HaloTag-eGFP* fusion protein in neutrophils.
- Neutrophils arrive rapidly at the tailfin wound site within 15–30 minutes, whereas macrophages (*mpeg1: SNAPtag-DsRed*, excited at 559 nm, Wavelength 3) arrive hours later.
- Incubation in the dark preserves the covalent HaloTag-Cy5 signal, so recruited neutrophils simultaneously exhibit fluorescence from both HaloTag-Cy5 (630 nm) and genetically encoded eGFP (488 nm).
- Therefore, signals are first detected under excitation wavelengths 1 and 2, supporting Choice D.
}

